            0.11
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Both the ratios are proportional to each other. We denote this by"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.376,
            0.113,
            0.621,
            0.133
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_3_equation_2.jpg",
          "content": "8 : 4 : 2 : 1 : : 4 : 2 : 1 : 0 . 5 ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.137,
            0.785,
            0.158
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In general, when two ratios with multiple terms are proportional"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.389,
            0.162,
            0.61,
            0.182
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_3_equation_4.jpg",
          "content": "a : b : c : d : : p : q : r : s"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.186,
            0.21,
            0.205
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "then,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.433,
            0.205,
            0.564,
            0.238
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_3_equation_6.jpg",
          "content": "{ \\frac { a } { p } } = { \\frac { b } { q } } = { \\frac { c } { r } } = { \\frac { d } { s } } \\bullet"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.246,
            0.847,
            0.322
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 1:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " To make a special shade of purple, paint must be mixed in the ratio, Red : Blue : White : : 2 : 3 : 5. If Yasmin has 10 litres of white paint, how many litres of red and blue paint should she add to get the same shade of purple?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.326,
            0.72,
            0.347
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the ratio 2 : 3 : 5, the white paint corresponds to 5 parts."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.349,
            0.592,
            0.37
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If 5 parts is 10 litres, 1 part is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "10 \\div 5 = 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " litres."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.352,
            0.373,
            0.645,
            0.394
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_3_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{Red}=2\\mathrm{parts}=2\\times2=4\\mathrm{stress}."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.349,
            0.396,
            0.648,
            0.416
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_3_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{Ble}=3\\mathrm{parts}=3\\times2=6\\mathrm{liters}."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.42,
            0.847,
            0.459
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, the purple paint will have 4 litres of red, 6 litres of blue, and 10 litres of white paint."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.467,
            0.596,
            0.49
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is the total volume of this purple paint?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.492,
            0.689,
            0.513
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The total volume of purple paint is 4 + 6 + 10 = 20 litres."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.523,
            0.847,
            0.653
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 2:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Cement concrete is a mixture of cement, sand, and gravel, and is widely used in construction. The ratio of the components in the mixture varies depending on how strong the structure needs to be. For structures that need greater strength like pillars, beams, and roofs, the ratio is 1 : 1.5 : 3, and the construction is also reinforced with steel rods. Using this ratio, if we have 3 bags of cement, how many bags of concrete mixture can we make?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.657,
            0.501,
            0.676
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The concrete mixture is in the ratio"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.222,
            0.681,
            0.775,
            0.702
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Bags of cement : bags of sand : bags of gravel :: 1 : 1.5 : 3."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.705,
            0.846,
            0.742
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If we have 3 bags of cement, we have to multiply the other terms by 3. So, the ratio is"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.333,
            0.742,
            0.663,
            0.761
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_3_equation_19.jpg",
          "content": "{ \\mathsf { c e m e n t : s a n d : g r a v e l : : 3 : 4 . 5 : 9 . } }"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.766,
            0.647,
            0.787
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In total, we have "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3+4.5+9=16.5"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " bags of concrete."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.808,
            0.662,
            0.832
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3.4 Dividing a Whole in a Given Ratio"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.842,
            0.847,
            0.916
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In an earlier chapter, we learnt how to divide a whole in a ratio, e.g., 12 in the ratio 2 : 1. To do this, we add the terms "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(2 + 1 = 3)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and divide the whole by this sum "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(12 \\div 3 = 4)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . We multiply each term by this quotient : "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 \\times 4 = 8"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 \\times 4 = 4"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . So, 12 divided in the ratio 2 : 1 is 8 : 4."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.913,
            0.121,
            0.935
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "58"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
